> A train ticket costs $63. A travel pass gives one third off the ticket price. A booking fee of $4.50 is then added to each ticket. A traveller buys 2 tickets using the pass. What is the total cost, to the nearest cent? Show the steps.

[Start thinking]

We need to compute total cost. Ticket price $63. Pass gives one third off the ticket price => discount = 1/3 of $63 = $21, so discounted price = $63 - $21 = $42 per ticket. Then booking fee $4.50 added to each ticket. So per ticket cost = $42 + $4.50 = $46.50. For 2 tickets: $46[0m
